# calendarAPI — separate app

- **`calendarAPI/` is not part of REACT-ADMIN.** It is the cloned repo [khaCey/calendarAPI](https://github.com/khaCey/calendarAPI) — a standalone Google Apps Script project for local editing and `clasp` pull/push.
- **Default:** `calendarAPI/` is listed in `.gitignore`. Do not `git add`, commit, or push it from the REACT-ADMIN root unless you are deliberately tracking it in REACT-ADMIN (see below).

## When making GAS changes in this workspace (agent or manual)

1. **Temporarily remove** the `calendarAPI/` line from `.gitignore` if you need REACT-ADMIN’s git to see the folder (rare).
2. Edit files under `calendarAPI/` as needed, or sync with **`clasp pull`** / **`clasp push`** from `calendarAPI/`.
3. When finished, **restore** `calendarAPI/` in `.gitignore` if you removed it so the nested repo stays untracked by REACT-ADMIN by default.
4. **Remind the user** to deploy from the Apps Script editor or `clasp push` + new Web App version when the live URL must pick up changes.

If the folder is not present locally, run `git clone https://github.com/khaCey/calendarAPI.git calendarAPI` from the REACT-ADMIN root, or paste edits into script.google.com.

## Secrets

- Do **not** commit `BOOKING_API_KEY`, poll keys, webhook URLs, or credentials inside `calendarAPI/` files. Use **Apps Script → Project settings → Script properties** (and `migratePropertiesFromConfig_()` / `getBookingApiKey_()` patterns in `Code.js`). Keep `Config.js` in Git with **empty strings** for secrets; configure locally or in Script properties only.
